# Take ownership with main.roc

**Prerequisites:** [Commands and live updates](/docs/tutorials/commands-and-live/).
**You will learn:** when to leave generated standalone dispatch, and how a
directory app reuses `.rocci` modules.
**Starting files:** [Datastar gallery](/examples/datastar/) (normal pattern
gallery) and [Snake](/examples/snake/) (advanced stress example).
**Time:** about twenty minutes.
**Verify:** `rocci run examples/rocci/custom/datastar --no-window` serves
`/search`.
**Next:** [Ship the application](/docs/tutorials/ship/).

Generated standalone apps are the right default. Switch to authored `main.roc`
when you need custom routing, extra platform effects, or a shape the generator
does not cover. Reuse `.rocci` components either way.

## Directory apps

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- run examples/rocci/custom/datastar --no-window
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8000/search | grep -E 'search|datastar'
```

`rocci run` on a directory compiles sibling `.rocci` modules and starts the
authored Roc program. `@view` / `@patch` on those modules are not the
generated standalone dispatcher; `main.roc` owns HTTP.

Read the gallery source index: [datastar source](/examples/datastar/source/).
Patterns:

| Route | What to notice |
| --- | --- |
| `/search` | `@let`, `@if`, `@for` |
| `/edit` | `@match` for editing |
| `/todos` | filters and lists |
| `/tabs` | lazy tabs |
| `/validate` | inline validation |

The server still owns HTML. Datastar remains transport.

## Snake is the ceiling

[Snake](/examples/snake/) is an explicitly advanced multiplayer stress
example with a hand-written SSE unfold. Do not copy that unfold into ordinary
apps; generated `@live` already emits the poll loop. Use Snake when you need a
custom ceiling the generator does not cover.

## Ability checklist

- Run a directory app rather than a single `.rocci` file
- Know that custom `main.roc` opts out of generated standalone dispatch
- Treat Snake as advanced, not as the second tutorial

Next: [ship](/docs/tutorials/ship/).
